    "paragraph": "Three of today's papers carry the tag \"Urban Transport and Accessibility\", exploring how remote work exposure affected Dutch inter-municipal relocation networks, sequencing mobile environmental exposure and travel stress in Singapore, and analyzing mobility-derived urban vitality data across 30 Chinese cities to identify spatiotemporal scaling laws. Outside this group, another study analyzed the drivers of intercity university-industry co-patenting in China's Yangtze River Delta from 2006 to 2020. Finally, a separate paper analyzed the distribution and drivers of county-level local government bonds across 2,507 Chinese county-level administrative units for the year 2022.",
